WEBVTT

1
00:00:07.600 --> 00:00:13.300
Every game lives on The Logic Grid's game cards. Tap Picture Grid to open it.

2
00:00:13.500 --> 00:00:21.900
Choose a difficulty. Basic is a 5×5 picture to learn on. Each level grows the grid and the logic, up to Master at 25×25.

3
00:00:22.100 --> 00:00:27.800
Pick a grid size, or tap Today's puzzle: one fresh picture for everyone, every day.

4
00:00:28.400 --> 00:00:35.600
More options: silent mode, sound effects, puzzles tuned to how you play, crossing out finished lines for you, and highlighting.

5
00:00:35.800 --> 00:00:42.100
We'll play an Easy 10×10. Tap Start puzzle: it's built just for you, with exactly one answer.

6
00:00:45.600 --> 00:00:52.200
Each puzzle has a title and a short story. The timer and your progress sit on the right.

7
00:00:52.400 --> 00:00:58.700
Shade cells so every row and column matches its numbers. When they all match, a picture appears.

8
00:00:58.900 --> 00:01:05.200
The numbers by each row and above each column are its runs of shaded cells, in order.

9
00:01:05.400 --> 00:01:12.600
Column 2 says 1 2: a run of 1, then a gap, then a run of 2. The gaps can be any size, but at least one cell.

10
00:01:12.800 --> 00:01:19.100
A 0 means nothing in that line is shaded. A line's numbers turn faint once it matches.

11
00:01:19.300 --> 00:01:28.400
Tap a cell to shade it with the Shade pen. Drag along a row or column to mark a whole stretch at once.

12
00:01:28.600 --> 00:01:35.800
Switch to the Cross pen to mark cells you know are blank. Tap a marked cell again to clear it.

13
00:01:39.000 --> 00:01:48.000
Row 3 (6) has 10 cells. However its runs slide, they always cover columns 5, 6.

14
00:01:48.300 --> 00:01:57.300
Row 5 (6) has 10 cells. However its runs slide, they always cover columns 5, 6.

15
00:01:57.600 --> 00:02:06.600
Row 6 (8) has 10 cells. However its runs slide, they always cover columns 3, 4, 5, 6, 7, 8.

16
00:02:06.900 --> 00:02:15.900
Row 7 (6) has 10 cells. However its runs slide, they always cover columns 5, 6.

17
00:02:16.200 --> 00:02:24.900
That's the whole game: find a line where some cells are certain, mark them, and use them in the lines that cross. No guessing, ever.

18
00:02:28.100 --> 00:02:32.300
Stuck? Hint shows a line you can work on now.

19
00:02:32.500 --> 00:02:38.200
Ask again and it explains why, then it can fill in the cells for you.

20
00:02:40.000 --> 00:02:46.600
Let's shade a wrong cell on purpose. Check marks wrong marks in red, and leaves everything else alone.

21
00:02:46.800 --> 00:02:53.100
Undo takes it back. Or switch on Show mistakes as I play to see them straight away.

22
00:02:53.300 --> 00:03:02.900
Rules and keys keeps the rules close by: Space shades, X crosses. Print the puzzle, save it to a file, or start a new one from here too.

23
00:03:06.300 --> 00:03:10.800
Keep working line by line until every row and column matches.

24
00:03:12.300 --> 00:03:16.500
Every line matches, and the picture is yours.

25
00:03:16.900 --> 00:03:23.800
Solved! Tell the game how it felt. Your answer, and how you played, tune the next puzzle to you.

26
00:03:24.000 --> 00:03:30.300
Watch the solution replays the logic one line at a time, with the reason for each step.

27
00:03:30.900 --> 00:03:38.100
Next puzzle is always new: you never see the same puzzle twice. Share my result sends your time to friends.

28
00:03:38.700 --> 00:03:44.700
Every picture you uncover joins Your picture gallery, next to your saved puzzles, stats and badges.
